      en: "The RTNB Building, completed in 1984, is the headquarters of Burundi's national broadcaster. The 12-story concrete tower rises 45 meters above Bujumbura's skyline. Funded by Chinese aid, it houses radio and television studios, transmission facilities, and administrative offices. The building's blue-tinted glass facade is a local landmark. RTNB broadcasts 18 hours daily in Kirundi, French, and Swahili. Its FM network includes 12 transmitters across the country, reaching an estimated 80% of the population. The building underwent seismic retrofitting in 2016 to improve resilience. An adjacent annex built in 2008 houses additional production studios.",
